*\n\nAfter making this change, run `ansible-lint` again. The “truthy value” error\nwill no longer appear, and the playbook will pass the length check for the\n`repo` string.\n\nIf you still see the error after this change, double‑check that there are no\nother `when` clauses that use a variable without a proper boolean test. In\nthat case, you can rewrite them as:\n\n```yaml\nwhen: hashicorp_version is defined          # installs a specific version\nwhen: hashicorp_version is not defined      # installs the latest\n```\n\nBoth of these are already boolean expressions, so `ansible‑lint` should accept\nthem once the long line is broken up.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'gpt-oss:20b', 'created_at': '2025-10-10T20:40:02.521506243Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 132793183467, 'load_duration': 157101401, 'prompt_eval_count': 891, 'prompt_eval_duration': 480351237, 'eval_count': 12940, 'eval_duration': 132154026535, 'model_name': 'gpt-oss:20b'} id='run--c376cda5-a89e-482c-afa9-76fe708b904b-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 891, 'output_tokens': 12940, 'total_tokens': 13831}
